---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import { url } from '../../lib/url'
import schema from '../../data/schema.json'
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What these plugins will and will not send, and how it is enforced." docs>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    These run on checkout pages, so the rules live in the shared core, not in individual plugins —
    and the test suite fails a release that breaks one.
    <a href={url('/sandbox/')}>Watch them work →</a>
  </p>

  <div class="scroll-x">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">No payment data</th>
          <td>Card number, CVV, expiry and billing address are stripped at any nesting depth, even when the platform's own payload includes them. Plugins read event payloads, never DOM inputs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">PII is opt-in</th>
          <td><code>usr.id</code> is the platform customer ID — that is all, by default. Email and name need an explicit flag. Phone and address have no flag at all.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Search terms as length</th>
          <td><code>search_term_length</code>, never the text. A shopper can type anything into a search box.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Free text dropped</th>
          <td>Notes, comments and messages are removed wherever they appear.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Nothing before consent</th>
          <td>A consent plugin sets <code>trackingConsent</code> to <code>not-granted</code> before the SDK starts, which stops RUM collecting anything. Pending events are dropped, not queued, so a later grant never backfills them.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Size caps</th>
          <td><code>items[]</code> opt-in and capped at {schema.limits.maxItems}; strings truncated at {schema.limits.maxStringLength}; objects deeper than four levels dropped.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">One order, counted once</th>
          <td><code>commerce.purchase</code> is deduplicated per <code>transaction_id</code> for {schema.limits.dedupeTtlHours} hours. No <code>transaction_id</code> means no purchase is sent at all.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Hooks cannot widen it</th>
          <td>A <code>beforeTrack</code> hook's output is re-filtered, so it cannot reintroduce a blocked attribute.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What a declined visitor means</h2>
  <p>
    They send nothing at all, so RUM cannot report opt-in rate. A consent plugin describes the
    categories of sessions that <em>did</em> opt in — never the share of visitors who did.
  </p>

  <h2>Declared footprint</h2>
  <p>
    Each plugin lists the globals it reads, events it subscribes to, storage keys it writes and RUM
    APIs it calls. The test suite compares that list against what the plugin actually did, so it
    cannot quietly call something undeclared. It is on every plugin page, and in the console with
    <code>debug: true</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Supply chain</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Published from CI only, with npm provenance.</li>
    <li>CDN URLs are exact-version with an SRI hash. No <code>latest</code> URL.</li>
    <li>GitHub Actions pinned by commit SHA, <code>persist-credentials: false</code>.</li>
    <li>A new runtime dependency needs maintainer review. The launch plugins have none beyond the core.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
  <p>
    Data leaving the browser that shouldn't, or a consent bypass, goes to
    <a href="https://github.com/kyletaylored/datadog-rum-community-plugins/security/advisories/new">a
    private security advisory</a> — not a public issue. Redact real payloads first.
  </p>

  <div class="next-cards">
    <a class="card" href={url('/sandbox/')}>
      <h3>See it enforced</h3>
      <p>Withhold consent and watch every event get refused.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href={url('/docs/schema/')}>
      <h3>Event schema</h3>
      <p>Every attribute, with its type and origin.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</Base>
